# Cheatsheet

Quick lookup for surfaces, the raster, fonts, formats, and device helpers. For concepts see [Building a Surface](surfaces.md).

## Surfaces
{: .col-2}

### A surface module

```elixir
defmodule MyDevice.Surface do
  use RasterExRatatui.Surface,
    app: MyDevice.App,
    format: RasterExRatatui.PixelFormat.RGB565,
    scale: 2

  @impl true
  def init(opts), do: {:ok, [size: {480, 320}], open_device(opts)}

  @impl true
  def push(patches, device), do: write_all(device, patches)
end
```

### Options

```elixir
app: MyApp               # required, an ExRatatui.App
app_opts: [...]          # passed to mount/1
size: {w, h}             # required (use, start_link, or init/1)
format: Mono             # required
font: Default6x8         # default
scale: 1                 # integer magnification
format_opts: [...]       # palette or tone thresholds
push_mode: :patches      # or :frame
min_interval: 0          # ms between pushes
shutdown_timeout: 4_000  # then the app server is killed
name: MyDevice.Surface
```

### Callbacks

```elixir
init(opts)            # {:ok, extra_opts, state} | {:stop, reason}
push(pixels, state)   # [%Patch{}] | {:frame, bin} -> state
handle_info(msg, st)  # {:noreply, st} | {:events, [event], st}
terminate(reason, st)
```

### Runtime API

```elixir
Surface.send_event(surface, %Key{code: "enter", kind: "press"})
Surface.resize(surface, {1280, 720})   #=> {cols, rows}
Surface.server(surface)                #=> app server pid
Surface.raster(surface) |> Raster.frame()
```

## Raster (pure)
{: .col-2}

### Build and size the session

```elixir
raster = Raster.new(size: {400, 300}, format: Mono)
{cols, rows} = Raster.grid_size(raster)        # {66, 37}
session = CellSession.new(cols, rows,
  font_size: Raster.font_size(raster))         # {6, 8}
Raster.margin(raster)                          # {4, 4}
```

### Fold diffs

```elixir
:ok = CellSession.draw(session, widgets)
diff = CellSession.take_cells_diff(session)
{raster, patches} = Raster.apply(raster, diff)
frame = Raster.frame(raster)   # width * height packed pixels
```

### Patches

```elixir
%Patch{x: 12, y: 0, width: 6, height: 8, data: bytes}
# write in list order; data is row-major, no stride padding
Patch.blit(frame, frame_width, bytes_per_pixel, patch)
```

## Fonts and formats
{: .col-2}

### Fonts

```elixir
Default6x8.cell_size()          # {6, 8}
Default6x8.glyph(?A)            # <<_::48>>
Art.parse(art, {8, 16}, pad: {0, 2})
Generated.braille({8, 16})      # %{cp => bits}
Generated.hatched({8, 16})      # placeholder
```

### Formats

```elixir
Mono       # 1 byte, 0 ink / 255 paper, Bayer dither
RGB565     # 2 bytes, little-endian
XRGB8888   # 4 bytes: b, g, r, 255

format_opts: [reset_fg: {229, 229, 229}, reset_bg: {0, 0, 0},
              theme: %{red: {255, 85, 85}}, bold_bright: true]
format_opts: [ink_max: 76, paper_min: 178]   # Mono
```

## Device helpers
{: .col-2}

### Framebuffer

```elixir
{:ok, fb} = Framebuffer.open("fb0")
fb.info   # %{width, height, bits_per_pixel, stride}
{:ok, format} = Framebuffer.format_for(fb.info)
:ok = Framebuffer.write(fb, patches)   # or {:frame, bin}
Framebuffer.unbind_console("vtcon1")
Framebuffer.blank("fb0", true)
```

### Evdev keyboards

```elixir
keyboard = Evdev.new(layout: :us)
{keyboard, keys} =
  Evdev.translate_all(keyboard, events)
# [%Key{code: "A", kind: "press", modifiers: ["shift"]}]
```
